  <p class="standfirst">Most brands already know what they should be publishing. The gap is execution, and in the age of AI search, that gap compounds.</p>

  <section class="tldr" aria-label="Summary">
    <h2>TL;DR</h2>
    <p>Content is important but rarely urgent, so it gets postponed, and the cost only shows up a year later, when a competitor has a library of useful answers and you don't. AI search raises the stakes, because AI systems understand your brand through the body of content that exists about you.</p>
    <p>The fix isn't another content calendar. It's a system you run in 90-day sprints: <strong>monitor, create, optimize, publish, learn</strong>, then make each cycle smarter than the last.</p>
  </section>

